 ## Storage
 
-Sessions live in Postgres ([keep sessions in the database](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md)).
+Sessions live in a signed cookie, not a server-side store
+([keep sessions in signed cookies](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md)).
+
+## Logout
+
+`logout(member_id)` in `larder/sessions.py` lets a volunteer end a member's session right away, for a stolen phone or
+similar emergency, instead of waiting out the 30-minute expiry. It only takes effect on the server a volunteer calls
+it on; since the two servers behind the load balancer share no store, the member stays logged in on the other server
+until their session there expires on its own. Rotating `LARDER_SESSION_KEY` logs out every member on every server at
+once ([keep sessions in signed cookies](../adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-signed-cookies.md)).
 
